<$fill $name="body">

!! Type a node

# In a Streams outline, right-click the node's drag handle.
# Click ''Kind type ▸'' to open the flyout submenu.
# Pick a type from the list (✓ marks the current one). The node now carries a `kind.type` field and shows a pill.

!! Edit a typed node's fields

# Click the pill on a typed node.
# The type's stream-fields appear inline on the same row; click a field to edit it.
# Use the ✎ toggle to switch between popup and inline editing; click ▾ to collapse.

!! Turn the pills off

Set `$:/config/rimir/kind-streams/enable` to `no` (or untick the box in the settings tab). Nodes render normally; you can still assign types from the right-click menu.

!! Change which fields show inline

The inline bar reuses kind's stream-fields for the type. Edit the type's `kind.stream-fields` (in kind's type builder) to control which fields appear — an empty list shows just the type pill.

</$fill>
</$transclude>
